#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180626} :activity/id #uuid "171b476e-9322-594d-b1d2-c603a90f1b67" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048207 :topic/id #uuid "886ced30-c0cc-548f-90c0-8a84697856ec" :topic/math-academy-id 3680} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180626 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180777 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to solve the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n2 - 4.5\n$$\n\nWe can solve this problem using a number line.\n\nTo subtract $4.5$ from $2$, we break up $4.5$ into its whole number part ($4$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- First, we subtract the whole number part. We start at $2$ on the number line and move $4$ places to the left, which brings us to $-2$.\n- Then, we subtract the decimal part. We move the remaining $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-2.5$.\n\n![](images/e7/e79d6ec2413d47e2b2b67237194a057d802746d1b9b016dcf118ca91b2bf31df.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2 - 4.5 = -2.5\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "1e60ed87-2f30-5d4d-9d0b-990a5f1b8e1f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8384 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "8566447b-d96f-5adc-9b6e-c089a3f423a4" :step/math-academy-id 75114 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180627}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180627 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179812 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179458 :question/id #uuid "0e9e4dd1-3161-5d3c-afab-5514e1c2d0d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-13383"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44b96053-1ffa-56d3-8129-15ada765b9a7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048549} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048911} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049097}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180189} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180191}] :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Decimals With Halves"} :step/id #uuid "6c4541f7-07d8-51f6-b705-9bb2d82f1069" :step/math-academy-id 75115 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180628}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180628 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180778 :tutorial/content "We can use the same methods that we learned to subtract whole numbers in more complicated situations.\n\nAs an example, let's consider the following problem:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{3.5}} - {\\color{blue}{9.8}}\n$$\n\nWe're subtracting a *positive* decimal from a smaller *positive* decimal. So the final answer must be negative.\n\nWe start by solving the following easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction *in the reverse order*:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{9.8}} - {\\color{red}{3.5}} = 6.3\n$$\n\nHowever, since our final answer must be negative, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{3.5}} - {\\color{blue}{9.8}} = -6.3\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b35021fd-095a-5cca-9a9e-24ce11a93ae2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8385 :tutorial/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Positive Decimals"} :step/id #uuid "56a03151-c084-5924-9eca-03e11afc4c98" :step/math-academy-id 75118 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180629}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180629 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180779 :tutorial/content "Now suppose we have the following problem:\n$-3.2 - 6.4$\nIn this case, we're subtracting a *positive* decimal from a *negative* decimal. So the final answer must be negative.\n\nWe start by solving the following easier problem, which is to *add their absolute values*:\n\n$$\n3.2+6.4 = 9.6\n$$\n\nHowever, since our final answer must be negative, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-3.2 - 6.4 = -9.6\n$$\n\n**Remember**\n\n- When we subtract a *positive* number from a smaller *positive* number, we carry out the subtraction *in the reverse order* and then make the final answer negative.\n- When we subtract a *positive* number from a *negative* number, we *add their absolute values* and then make the final answer negative." :tutorial/id #uuid "93e4bd99-076c-5ac9-9c1b-362ae1e66e8f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8386 :tutorial/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Negative Decimals"} :step/id #uuid "a503405f-0d74-5b80-9c37-8d32b6f8da23" :step/math-academy-id 75119 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180630}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180630 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179813 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179459 :question/id #uuid "6bd42661-9814-51ce-a359-39bd54aff3e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13384"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "507d4d46-699c-5b4f-a010-66aec6abef67" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179935}] :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Decimals"} :step/id #uuid "96ee8d90-d6bf-59b8-a1c3-bf6554a1e0f9" :step/math-academy-id 75120 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180631}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180631 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179814 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179460 :question/id #uuid "45b45968-91b2-5ed4-86c2-51d31e02b714" :question/math-academy-id "e-13385"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "778ae1c8-c651-56f1-ab58-1817d3fe4bb9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048588}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179938} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179939}] :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Decimals With Unequal Numbers of Decimals"} :step/id #uuid "ef013d16-ba95-5bba-b84c-4f5db1abc151" :step/math-academy-id 75123}] :activity/title "Subtracting a Positive Decimal From a Smaller Decimal" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179836}]}
